1
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:06,871
This video shows you how to make your browser trust your leader's certificate,

2
00:00:06,871 --> 00:00:09,310
so smeltr opens with no warning.

3
00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:12,960
Chrome warns, because your leader signed its own certificate,

4
00:00:12,960 --> 00:00:15,430
with an authority Chrome doesn't know.

5
00:00:15,480 --> 00:00:19,628
Go past the warning one last time, and sign in.

6
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:26,513
In Admin, open System, then Leader certificate.

7
00:00:26,513 --> 00:00:31,745
Under Current authority is the authority that signed the leader's certificate,

8
00:00:31,745 --> 00:00:33,470
with its fingerprint.

9
00:00:33,520 --> 00:00:37,230
Download its certificate, ca.pem.

10
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:40,393
Before you trust it, make sure it's your leader's.

11
00:00:40,393 --> 00:00:44,070
On the leader's host, print the fingerprint of its copy.

12
00:00:44,120 --> 00:00:48,190
On your laptop, print the fingerprint of the file you downloaded.

13
00:00:48,240 --> 00:00:52,150
They match, so the file is your leader's own authority.

14
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:56,494
Chrome on Linux trusts the authorities in your certificate database.

15
00:00:56,494 --> 00:00:58,294
Add this one there.

16
00:01:00,240 --> 00:01:05,230
On Windows or macOS, add it to the system's trust store instead.

17
00:01:05,280 --> 00:01:08,935
Restart Chrome, and open smeltr again.

18
00:01:09,360 --> 00:01:12,501
Your workers trusted this authority from the start.

19
00:01:12,501 --> 00:01:14,630
Their enrollment code named it.

20
00:01:14,680 --> 00:01:16,506
Check on learning.

21
00:01:16,706 --> 00:01:19,041
The page showed a fingerprint too.

22
00:01:19,041 --> 00:01:21,976
Why check it on the leader's host?

23
00:01:26,376 --> 00:01:30,233
You downloaded it over a connection your browser doesn't trust yet,

24
00:01:30,233 --> 00:01:35,299
so someone in the middle could have swapped both the file and the fingerprint beside it.

25
00:01:35,299 --> 00:01:39,756
The file on the leader's host never travelled over that connection.

26
00:01:40,656 --> 00:01:44,402
Next, you order a certificate over ACME.
